.TH PI-STACK 1 "July 2026" "pi-stack" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pi-stack \- run the pi coding agent in a Docker sandbox and manage its host services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pi-stack
.RI [ \-\-profile\ NAME ]
.br
.B pi-stack
.RI [ \-\-profile\ NAME ]
.B run
.RI [ DIR ]
.RI [ flags ]
.RI [ \-\- " pi-args..." ]
.br
.B pi-stack
.RI [ \-\-profile\ NAME ]
.I DIR
.br
.B pi-stack
.RI [ \-\-profile\ NAME ]
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pi-stack
is the launcher for the
.B pi
coding agent in a Docker Sandbox managed by
.BR sbx (1).
It also controls the host-side memory service on port 11435 and knowledge
service on port 11436.
.PP
With no command,
.B pi-stack
shows status.  It never launches a sandbox.  Launching is explicit through
.B run
or through the bare existing-directory form.  On a host without a configuration
file, the no-argument form first offers setup when attached to a terminal.
A bare non-directory word is an error, not a workspace name.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "status, st"
.TP
.BR "pi-stack status" " [" \-\-json "]"
Show a read-only snapshot of services, provider keys, knowledge bundles, MCP
registration, the active profile, and running
.B pi-stack-*
sandboxes.  The
.B \-\-json
option emits the snapshot as JSON.  This is also the no-command action.
.SS setup
.TP
.BR "pi-stack setup" " [" \-\-account " " email "] [" \-\-knowledge " " path-or-url "] [" \-\-yes "|" \-y "|" \-\-non-interactive "]"
Run idempotent first-run setup, write configuration, seed the 1Password refs
template, and register configured MCP servers.
.B \-\-account
sets the Google Workspace account.
.B \-\-knowledge
scaffolds or selects the global OKF bundle.
.BR \-\-yes ,
.BR \-y ,
and
.B \-\-non-interactive
suppress prompts and print unfinished steps as commands.
.SS doctor
.TP
.BR "pi-stack doctor" " [" \-\-json "]"
Check provider keys, Ollama and its configured models, memory, Google Workspace,
1Password refs, and MCP registrations.  Print repair commands for failed checks.
.B \-\-json
emits a machine-readable report.
.SS run
.TP
.BR "pi-stack run" " [" DIR "] [" \-\-dev "] [" \-\-skills " " DIR "]... [" \-\-kit " " K "]... [" \-\-mcp " " M "]... [" \-\-name " " N "] [" \-\-model " " M "] [" \-\- " " pi-args... "]"
Launch a sandbox for
.IR DIR ,
which defaults to the current directory.  An explicit directory must exist.
Arguments after
.B \-\-
are passed to
.BR pi .
.TP
.B \-\-dev
Use the local checkout kit and load its skills live.  A checkout must be found
through
.BR PI_STACK_DEV_ROOT ,
the current directory or an ancestor, or the launcher's installed location.
.TP
.BI \-\-skills " DIR"
Mount and load an additional skill tree.  Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-kit " K"
Replace automatic kit selection with a path or git URL.  Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-mcp " M"
Attach an MCP server when creating the sandbox.  Repeatable; attachment is used
only when
.B SBX_MCP_URL
is set.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " N"
Use
.I N
as the sandbox name.  Otherwise the launcher derives
.BI pi-stack- workspace
and appends a non-default profile name.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " M"
Pass
.I M
to
.B pi
as its active model.
.SS serve
.TP
.BR "pi-stack serve" " [" args... "]"
Execute
.B pi-stack-host serve
with unchanged arguments.  With no service arguments, the host configuration
selects services.  Memory is enabled by default; knowledge runs when enabled.
.TP
.B "pi-stack serve stop"
Read the supervisor pidfile and verify that the process is
.BR "pi-stack-host serve"
before sending SIGTERM.  If neither /proc nor ps can identify the process, it
REFUSES to signal (remove the pidfile to override) rather than trust the pidfile
alone.  It sends SIGKILL only if the process does not exit after about five
seconds and a repeated identity check still confirms the process is ours.
Extra arguments are rejected.
.TP
.BR "pi-stack serve status" " [" \-\-json "]"
Report the supervisor PID and memory and knowledge port state.
.B \-\-json
emits JSON.
.SS memory
The aliases
.BR mem ,
.BR search ,
.BR add ,
.BR rm ,
.BR promotable ,
and
.B status
map respectively to
.BR memory ,
.BR recall ,
.BR remember ,
.BR forget ,
.BR learnings ,
and
.BR stats .
.TP
.BR "pi-stack memory recall" " " query " [" \-\-limit " " N "] [" \-\-project " " P "] [" \-\-json "]"
Search stored facts.  The default limit is 8.  The default project filter is
empty.  Short aliases
.B \-n
and
.B \-p
are accepted for
.B \-\-limit
and
.BR \-\-project .
.TP
.BR "pi-stack memory remember" " " text... " [" \-\-json "]"
Store a fact with source
.B cli
in the active profile.
.TP
.BR "pi-stack memory forget" " " id " [" \-\-json "]"
Delete the fact matching an ID or ID prefix in the active profile.  The
.B \-\-json
option emits the raw result.
.TP
.BR "pi-stack memory learnings" " [" \-\-min " " N "] [" \-\-json "]"
List recurring, promotable learnings.  The default minimum frequency is 3.
.TP
.BR "pi-stack memory stats" " [" \-\-json "]"
Print counts by kind and durability for the active profile.
.PP
Memory RPC commands return status 3 when the memory daemon cannot be reached.
Full backup and restore are now the top-level
.B backup
and
.B restore
verbs, not memory subcommands.
.SS backup
.TP
.BR "pi-stack backup" " [" \-\-out " " PATH "] [" \-\-keep " " N "]"
Create a hot, verified FULL backup, safe while
.B serve
holds the database.  It packages a SQLite
.B "VACUUM INTO"
snapshot of the memory database, the
.B config.toml
(profiles), the
.B op-refs.env
(references only), and a
.B manifest.json
(format version 2, recording the profile names and a note of each configured
knowledge bundle's path and git remote) into a gzip tar archive.  Knowledge
bundle contents are NOT archived: a bundle is a git repository and git is its
backup; the manifest records only where it lives.  The default output is
.BR ~/.pi-stack/backups/pi-stack-backup- timestamp .tar.gz;
the default retention count is 7.  The alias
.B \-o
is accepted for
.BR \-\-out .
The command execes the sibling
.B pi-stack-host
binary and propagates its status.
.SS restore
.TP
.BR "pi-stack restore" " " archive " [" \-\-force "]"
Restore a FULL backup by safe swap.  The command refuses to run while the memory
service is listening and refuses to replace an existing database without
.BR \-\-force .
With
.B \-\-force
(the alias
.B \-f
is accepted), it moves the current database to a timestamped backup first.  The
.B config.toml
and
.B op-refs.env
are always moved aside to a timestamped
.B .bak
file before the archived versions are written, so profiles come back and the
change is reversible.  A format-version-1 (memory-only manifest) archive still
restores.  The command reports the restored memory rows, the config profiles now
present, and the recorded knowledge-bundle locations, then execes the sibling
.B pi-stack-host
binary and propagates its status.
.SS knowledge
The alias
.B kb
maps to
.BR knowledge ;
.B search
maps to
.BR query ;
and
.B push
maps to
.BR sync .
.TP
.BR "pi-stack knowledge init" " [" DIR "]"
Scaffold an OKF bundle, initialize Git when available, add it to
.BR knowledge_bundles ,
and enable the knowledge service.  The default directory is
.B knowledge
under the configuration directory.  Existing bundle files are not overwritten.
.TP
.BR "pi-stack knowledge use" " " path-or-git-url
Set a global bundle reference.  A local path is made absolute but is not checked
for existence or OKF contents.  A Git URL is cloned or updated below the
configuration directory in
.BR knowledge-cache .
.TP
.BR "pi-stack knowledge use" " " \-\-project " " path-or-git-url " [" \-\-dir " " D "]"
Write
.B .pi-stack/knowledge
under
.I D
(default current directory) without changing global configuration.
.TP
.BR "pi-stack knowledge ls" " [" \-\-json "]"
List the active profile's configured bundles, service state, and any project
pointer.  JSON output is selected with
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.BR "pi-stack knowledge query" " " text... " [" \-\-limit " " N "] [" \-\-json "]"
Search the daemon within the active profile's bundles.  The default limit is 5;
.B \-n
is an alias for
.BR \-\-limit .
An unreachable daemon returns status 3.
.TP
.BR "pi-stack knowledge sync" " [" \-m " " MSG "] [" \-\-bundle " " D "] [" \-\-allow-main "]"
Commit and push a bundle.  Without
.BR \-\-bundle ,
exactly one bundle must be configured for the active profile.  The default
commit message contains a UTC timestamp.  By default, create and push a
.B knowledge/sync-*
review branch and print a
.B gh pr create
hint.
.B \-\-allow-main
instead commits and pushes the current branch; detached HEAD is refused.
.B \-m
is an alias for
.BR \-\-message .
.TP
.BR "pi-stack knowledge remote" " [" \-\-bundle " " D "]"
Show the selected bundle's origin URL.
.TP
.BR "pi-stack knowledge remote set" " " url " [" \-\-bundle " " D "]"
Add or replace the selected bundle's origin URL.
.SS mcp
.TP
.BR "pi-stack mcp register" " [" name... "]"
Register named local stdio MCP servers with the sbx gateway.  With no names,
use the active profile's configured MCP list.  Remote gateway-catalog names are
skipped.  Registration requires
.BR SBX_MCP_URL .
.TP
.B "pi-stack mcp ls"
Execute
.BR "sbx mcp ls" .
If
.B sbx
is unavailable, print the command to run on the host.
.SS profile
The aliases
.B list
and
.B set
map to
.B ls
and
.BR use .
.TP
.BR "pi-stack profile ls" " [" \-\-json "]"
List configured profiles and mark the active profile.  With no profile
subcommand, this is the default action.
.TP
.BR "pi-stack profile use" " " name
Persist
.I name
as
.BR active_profile .
The name must already exist.  Use
.B default
to select the base configuration.
.SS secret
With no subcommand,
.B secret
runs
.BR status .
.TP
.B "pi-stack secret status"
Report whether
.B op
is installed and has an account, and classify configured refs without printing
secret values.
.TP
.B "pi-stack secret edit"
Create the refs-only template if absent, then open it with
.B VISUAL
or
.BR EDITOR .
If neither is set, print the path.
.TP
.B "pi-stack secret check"
Resolve each active
.B op://
reference using
.B op read
and print only OK or FAIL.  Missing refs state or unavailable
.B op
returns status 3; failed resolutions return status 1.
.SS config
With no subcommand,
.B config
runs
.BR show .
.TP
.B "pi-stack config show"
Print the resolved configuration path followed by decoded TOML with defaults
applied.
.TP
.BR "pi-stack config path" " [" op-refs "]"
Print the path to
.B config.toml
or, with
.BR op-refs ,
the path to
.BR op-refs.env .
.TP
.BR "pi-stack config set" " [" \-\-profile " " N "] " key " " value
Set a scalar key or add a value to a list key, then save the configuration.
.TP
.BR "pi-stack config unset" " [" \-\-profile " " N "] " key " [" value "]"
Clear or reset a scalar key, or remove
.I value
from a list key.
.PP
Base keys are
.BR gog_account ,
.BR mcp ,
.BR services ,
.BR knowledge_bundles ,
.BR memory_watcher_model ,
and
.BR memory_embed_model .
Per-profile keys are
.BR gog_account ,
.BR mcp ,
.BR knowledge_bundles ,
and
.BR kit
(the alias
.B kits
is accepted).  Profile writes create the named profile if absent.
.BR services ,
.BR memory_watcher_model ,
and
.B memory_embed_model
are global and reject
.BR \-\-profile .
Setting base
.B knowledge_bundles
enables the knowledge service.  A per-profile write does not; enable the global
.B knowledge
service separately.
.SS reset
.TP
.BR "pi-stack reset" " [" \-\-keep-memory "] [" \-\-sbx "] [" \-\-force "] [" \-\-yes "|" \-y "]"
Stop host services and move configuration and data aside to timestamped
.B .bak-*
siblings.  Nothing is hard-deleted.
.B \-\-keep-memory
preserves captured memory while resetting other state.
.B \-\-sbx
also attempts, on a best-effort basis, to remove all
.B pi-stack-*
sandboxes and unregister configured MCP servers.  Failures in those sbx actions
are reported but do not fail the reset.
.B \-\-force
allows data movement if the service still appears to be running.
.BR \-\-yes
or
.B \-y
suppresses confirmation and is required on a non-interactive terminal.
.SS uninstall
.TP
.BR "pi-stack uninstall" " [" \-\-keep-memory "] [" \-\-force "] [" \-\-yes "|" \-y "]"
Perform the reset action, then remove the installed
.B pi-stack
and
.B pi-stack-host
entries from
.B ~/.local/bin
only when they are symlinks to pi-stack binaries.  If reset fails, leave the
symlinks installed.
.SS "version"
.TP
.B "pi-stack version"
Print the stamped launcher version.  The aliases
.B \-v
and
.B \-\-version
are accepted.
.SS help
.TP
.BR "pi-stack help" " [" verb "]"
Print general help or the authoritative usage text for an implemented verb.
.B \-h
and
.B \-\-help
are top-level aliases.
.SS man
.TP
.B "pi-stack man"
Render this manual page.  The page is embedded in the binary, so no
.B MANPATH
entry is required.  The rendered page is produced through the first available
of
.BR mandoc (1),
.BR man (1),
or
.BR groff (1);
if none is present the raw roff source is written out.  When standard output is
not a terminal, the page is written directly without a pager, so
.B "pi-stack man"
can be piped or redirected.  The global alias
.B \-\-man
is accepted anywhere on the command line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
Select a named profile.  The option may appear before or after the command, but
must appear before a
.B \-\-
argument terminator.  The
.BI \-\-profile= NAME
form is also accepted.  An empty profile name is an error.  Commands that resolve a profile reject an
unknown name.  A profile-scoped
.B "config set"
or
.B "config unset"
may instead create the named profile.  Backup, restore, global knowledge
init/use, config show/path, setup, serve, version, and lifecycle file movement
are not profile-scoped.  For profile-aware commands, the option selects the
context used by run, status, doctor, memory RPCs, knowledge query/list/sync,
MCP registration, and profile configuration writes.
.SH PROFILES
A profile is a named override set layered on the base configuration.  It may
override
.BR gog_account ,
.BR mcp ,
.BR knowledge_bundles ,
and
.BR kits.stack .
A present list replaces the base list; an absent list inherits it.  The implicit
.B default
profile is the base configuration.
.PP
Selection precedence is:
.B \-\-profile
first,
.B PI_STACK_PROFILE
second,
.B active_profile
from configuration third, and
.B default
last.  The host supervisor indexes the union of knowledge bundles from all
profiles; queries are scoped to the selected profile.
.SH FILES
.SS "Configuration tree"
.TP
.B ~/.config/pi-stack/config.toml
Machine-managed TOML configuration.  The directory and file may move under
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
or
.BR PI_STACK_CONFIG .
Schema fields are
.BR version_pin ,
.BR services ,
.BR mcp ,
.BR active_profile ,
.BR memory_watcher_model ,
.BR memory_embed_model ,
.BR gog_account ,
.BR knowledge_bundles ,
.BR kits.stack ,
.BR skills.paths ,
.BR profiles.* ,
and
.BR plugins.* .
.TP
.B ~/.config/pi-stack/op-refs.env
Refs-only environment file for host MCP credentials.  Secret entries are
.B op://vault/item/field
references resolved by
.BR op (1).
.TP
.B ~/.config/pi-stack/broker-token
Mode-0600 bearer shared by launcher and host broker components.
.TP
.B ~/.config/pi-stack/serve.pid
PID of the running
.B pi-stack-host serve
supervisor.
.TP
.B ~/.config/pi-stack/knowledge/
Default global OKF bundle created by
.BR "knowledge init" .
.TP
.B ~/.config/pi-stack/knowledge-cache/
Cached clones for knowledge bundle Git URLs.
.SS "Data tree"
.TP
.B ~/.pi-stack/memory/memory.db
Default memory SQLite database.
.TP
.B ~/.pi-stack/knowledge/knowledge.db
Default knowledge SQLite index.
.TP
.B ~/.pi-stack/backups/pi-stack-backup-*.tar.gz
Default full backup archives (memory, config, and op-refs).
.SS "Workspace and installation files"
.TP
.B .pi-stack/knowledge
Committed per-project knowledge bundle pointer.
.TP
.B .pi-stack/knowledge.scope
Launcher-generated canonical bundle scope for the current run.
.TP
.B .pi-stack/profile
Launcher-generated active memory profile for the current run.
.TP
.B ~/.local/bin/pi-stack
Installed launcher symlink removed by
.BR uninstall .
.TP
.B ~/.local/bin/pi-stack-host
Installed host-service symlink removed by
.BR uninstall .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PI_STACK_CONFIG
Use this exact path for
.BR config.toml .
Its parent also contains
.BR op-refs.env ,
.BR broker-token ,
and
.BR serve.pid .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Use
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pi-stack
as the configuration directory when
.B PI_STACK_CONFIG
is unset.
.TP
.B PI_STACK_PROFILE
Select a profile when
.B \-\-profile
is absent.
.TP
.B PI_STACK_DEV_ROOT
Directory of a pi-stack checkout used by
.BR "run --dev" .
It must contain
.BR pi-kit/spec.yaml .
.TP
.B PI_STACK_DEBUG
When non-empty, print the composed
.B sbx
command before running it.
.TP
.B PI_STACK_OP_REFS
Override the refs file included by
.BR backup .
This does not change the canonical refs path used by
.BR "secret" .
.TP
.B MEMORY_DB
Override the memory database path, normally
.BR ~/.pi-stack/memory/memory.db .
Reset, backup, and restore honor it.
.TP
.B KNOWLEDGE_DB
Override the knowledge index path, normally
.BR ~/.pi-stack/knowledge/knowledge.db .
Reset honors it.
.TP
.B MEMORY_PORT
Override memory port 11435 for the host service, launcher RPC client, status,
reset guard, restore service probe, and serve control.
.TP
.B KNOWLEDGE_PORT
Override knowledge port 11436 for the host service, launcher RPC client, and
serve control.
.TP
.B MEMORY_WATCHER_MODEL
Override the Ollama fact-capture model.  The configuration default is
.BR gemma4 .
.TP
.B MEMORY_EMBED_MODEL
Override the Ollama embedding model used by memory and knowledge.  The
configuration default is
.BR nomic-embed-text .
.TP
.B KNOWLEDGE_BUNDLES
Comma- or platform path-list-separated bundle paths used by the host supervisor
only when configured knowledge bundles, including profile bundles, are empty.
.TP
.B SBX_MCP_URL
Enable sbx MCP operations.  MCP registration requires it; run-time MCP
attachment is omitted when it is unset.
.TP
.B VISUAL
Editor used by
.BR "secret edit" .
Takes precedence over
.BR EDITOR .
.TP
.B EDITOR
Fallback editor used by
.BR "secret edit" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, displayed status, an accepted abort, or help.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration, filesystem, Git, subprocess, RPC-response, or other operational
failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command, option, argument, or other usage error.
.TP
.B 3
A required host service or secret-check dependency is unreachable.  Memory and
knowledge RPC commands use this status for a down daemon.
.PP
Commands that execute
.BR sbx ,
.BR pi-stack-host ,
or another child process may propagate that process's exit status.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run guided setup:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pi-stack setup
.RE
.fi
.PP
Launch the current directory, then launch a project under the work profile:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pi-stack run
pi-stack --profile work run ~/src/project
.RE
.fi
.PP
Recall and record memory:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pi-stack memory recall "release process" --limit 5
pi-stack memory remember "Release tags use the v prefix"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Push knowledge changes to a review branch:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pi-stack knowledge sync -m "knowledge: update release process"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Edit 1Password references and stop host services:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pi-stack secret edit
pi-stack serve stop
.RE
.fi
.PP
Reset state while preserving captured memory:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pi-stack reset --keep-memory
.RE
.fi
.PP
Back up and restore the full stack (memory, config, op-refs):
.PP
.nf
.RS
pi-stack backup --out ~/backups/pi-stack.tar.gz
pi-stack serve stop
pi-stack restore ~/backups/pi-stack.tar.gz --force
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pi (1),
.BR sbx (1),
.BR op (1)
